{
  "requirement": "The review prompt MUST include at least one worked example of a mechanical change and at least one worked example of a design question. The mechanical example MUST show a flawed draft together with the change the reviewer makes to it.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations** (`requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt.examples`):\n1. The review prompt MUST include at least one worked example of a mechanical change.\n2. The mechanical example MUST show a flawed draft together with the change the reviewer makes to it.\n3. The review prompt MUST include at least one worked example of a design question.\n\n**Test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_review_prompt_works_a_mechanical_example_and_a_design_question]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It reads the `## Examples` section of the skill's `references/review-prompt.md` through `review_prompt()` and `section`. It then calls `assert_text_in_order`, which requires each phrase to appear after the previous one.\n- `Compound, with a mechanical fix:` introduces the mechanical example (obligation 1).\n- `> The \\`refactor\\` command accepts` is the quoted flawed draft.\n- `Split into` is the reviewer's change. The draft must come before it, so the test covers obligation 2.\n- `Not a question` marks the fix as mechanical.\n- `A design question:`, then `Options:`, then `Recommend` require a design example with options and a recommendation (obligation 3).\n\nThe actual section in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md` has the quoted compound draft, the split, and a quoted design question with options (a) to (c) and a recommendation. The assertions are scoped to the Examples section. Deleting the draft, the fix or the design example would make the test fail.\n\nTo check content in a prompt document, phrase-presence and ordering assertions are an appropriate method. The test does not assert the second mechanical example, but the requirement only asks for at least one. I found no gaps.",
